e\": 1315}, {\"events\": 128, \"node\": 792}, {\"events\": 120, \"node\": 589}, {\"events\": 94, \"node\": 357}, {\"events\": 94, \"node\": 728}, {\"events\": 92, \"node\": 121}, {\"events\": 92, \"node\": 785}, {\"events\": 92, \"node\": 898}], \"window\": [64269, 94269]}", "latency_ms": 23, "tokens_before": 55550, "tokens_after": 55550, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_25544f86", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "regime_switch", "entities": [121, 357, 381, 594, 728, 785, 898, 1269, 1415, 1460, 1701, 1923], "window": [64269, 94269], "confidence": 0.87, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "At the prescribed half-window of 5000, the group's peak before/after contact dissimilarity is only 0.286 at t=88243 (step_01), far below the 0.6 threshold. The series is a smooth U-shape (0.19 -> 0.03 -> 0.29) with no step discontinuity \u2014 the signature of gradual background turnover, not a regime switch. The before/after sets at the peak differ by only a handful of nodes (316, 1020, 1353, 1710 out; 153, 399, 595, 953, 1315, 1457, 1549 in) against a stable core of ~30 shared partners.\n\nI tested three alternative explanations. (1) A narrower bandwidth of 2500 does produce spikes of 0.70 at t=78307 and 0.63 at t=80871 (step_10), but these are artifacts, not evidence: they fall exactly in the low-activity trough where unique edges halve from ~60 to 30 (step_03) and events drop from 193/203 to 101 (step_12). Node 1701 has literally zero contacts in that trough (step_13), so the 'after' set collapses to 9 nodes that are a strict SUBSET of the 30-node 'before' set \u2014 the neighbourhood thins and then recovers the same partners, rather than an old set being replaced by a new one. Immediately after, dissimilarity returns to 0.03. (2) The edge-level Jaccard of 0.0 across the wide 15k split (step_06) looks dramatic but is misleading: the partner identities are identical. Node 121 contacts {170,172,195,272,309,...,1897} early (step_07) and node 1923 contacts the same pool late (step_08). What rotates is which group member touches a fixed shared contact pool, not the pool itself \u2014 the opposite of a partner-set switch. (3) Volume and popularity do not explain a change either: no bursts at z=1.5 (step_09), uniform per-node degrees of ~30-34 partners and 90-94 events each (step_04), and the group members are ordinary mid-rank actors well below hub 1315 (step_14).\n\nAll members share one persistent contact pool for the entire 30k window; the only large excursion is a sparsity artifact in a documented activity trough. No abrupt regime switch is present."}, "raw_final_response": "The prescribed 5000-half-window analysis gives a peak dissimilarity of 0.286, well below 0.6.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_25544f86\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [121, 357, 381, 594, 728, 785, 898, 1269, 1415, 1460, 1701, 1923],\n  \"window\": [64269, 94269],\n  \"confidence\": 0.87,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"At the prescribed half-window of 5000, the group's peak before/after contact dissimilarity is only 0.286 at t=88243 (step_01), far below the 0.6 threshold. The series is a smooth U-shape (0.19 -> 0.03 -> 0.29) with no step discontinuity \u2014 the signature of gradual background turnover, not a regime switch. The before/after sets at the peak differ by only a handful of nodes (316, 1020, 1353, 1710 out; 153, 399, 595, 953, 1315, 1457, 1549 in) against a stable core of ~30 shared partners.\\n\\nI tested three alternative explanations. (1) A narrower bandwidth of 2500 does produce spikes of 0.70 at t=78307 and 0.63 at t=80871 (step_10), but these are artifacts, not evidence: they fall exactly in the low-activity trough where unique edges halve from ~60 to 30 (step_03) and events drop from 193/203 to 101 (step_12). Node 1701 has literally zero contacts in that trough (step_13), so the 'after' set collapses to 9 nodes that are a strict SUBSET of the 30-node 'before' set \u2014 the neighbourhood thins and then recovers the same partners, rather than an old set being replaced by a new one. Immediately after, dissimilarity returns to 0.03. (2) The edge-level Jaccard of 0.0 across the wide 15k split (step_06) looks dramatic but is misleading: the partner identities are identical. Node 121 contacts {170,172,195,272,309,...,1897} early (step_07) and node 1923 contacts the same pool late (step_08). What rotates is which group member touches a fixed shared contact pool, not the pool itself \u2014 the opposite of a partner-set switch. (3) Volume and popularity do not explain a change either: no bursts at z=1.5 (step_09), uniform per-node degrees of ~30-34 partners and 90-94 events each (step_04), and the group members are ordinary mid-rank actors well below hub 1315 (step_14).\\n\\nAll members share one persistent contact pool for the entire 30k window; the only large excursion is a sparsity artifact in a documented activity trough. No abrupt regime switch is present.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 66973, "total_output_tokens": 4494, "total_tokens": 71467, "total_latency_ms": 71606, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "tool_protocol_errors": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}